<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:45:13Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Carney says US trying to break Canada amid vote for Alberta independence referendum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a6062355f93f13cff8b74ff1facc110f6dc93d2343be2cbfc7c24fe261fb0a63</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:45:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T04:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/carney-says-us-trying-to-break-canada-amid-vote-for-alberta-independence-referendum/a-79675652--8df7b8da129e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/carney-says-us-trying-to-break-canada-amid-vote-for-alberta-independence-referendum/a-79675652?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The oil-rich province of Alberta will vote to decide if it wants to remain a Canadian province or start the legal process toward separation. Carney warned that the US was trying the divide-and-rule tactic.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Oregon school shooting: 3 children, teacher killed; 16-year-old gunman dies after community member pursues him into school</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3b24269323b54b92c41c65fb05b8bbb597549a374a4a9ec6851ee97256e8d7a6</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:45:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T21:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/oregon-school-shooting-3-children-teacher-killed-16-year-old-gunman-dies-after-community-member-purs/a-79674849--67eb9ee3350d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/oregon-school-shooting-3-children-teacher-killed-16-year-old-gunman-dies-after-community-member-pursues-him-into-school/a-79674849?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A 16-year-old gunman killed three children and a teacher at an elementary school in Bend, Oregon, and wounded two others. A community member pursued and killed the suspected shooter, authorities said.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bus, train collide, injuring 19 at Channel Tunnel terminal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:284109a1397f99aec1a1235d6e34beed72b49d6dcd64097a9cbef1c758e994bb</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:45:13Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T20:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bus-train-collide-injuring-19-at-channel-tunnel-terminal/a-79674671--04ade7f3eab7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bus-train-collide-injuring-19-at-channel-tunnel-terminal/a-79674671?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A minibus carrying truck drivers collided with a freight train near the Channel Tunnel entrance in France, injuring 19 people, two of them severely. Authorities launched an inquiry into what caused the accident.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Venezuela's Nicolas Maduro pleads not guilty to torture charges</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5ae324e0cccef7f5d9f3e38fa53902b04bf6f16c66003ed76c14b4910a519ea0</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T18:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/venezuela-s-nicolas-maduro-pleads-not-guilty-to-torture-charges/a-79673496--661837b93a79.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/venezuela-s-nicolas-maduro-pleads-not-guilty-to-torture-charges/a-79673496?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Maduro and his wife were charged with leading a state-sponsored repression campaign that tortured scores of victims during his presidency from 2013 to 2026.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Self-replicating AI: Is your fridge a cybersecurity risk?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f11bedc805d9c7d2258f932a004005e62933e8ca38b5eeb1e699c9bd59c3130b</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T18:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/self-replicating-ai-is-your-fridge-a-cybersecurity-risk/a-79662958--8f5eea61704f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/self-replicating-ai-is-your-fridge-a-cybersecurity-risk/a-79662958?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Anthropic researchers warn that AI worms could soon target connected household devices and spread from one device to another. Cyberattacks on French supermarkets illustrate just how vulnerable such systems can be.</summary><category term="Technology" /></entry><entry><title>Middle East updates: Houthis target Yemen government palace in Aden</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ced91f9c265852dd43b4bf6519bd4c1c8cc648d434dfc3cc9449ad3f63a8baa</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T17:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/middle-east-updates-houthis-target-yemen-government-palace-in-aden/live-79672880--01517cb5752d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/middle-east-updates-houthis-target-yemen-government-palace-in-aden/live-79672880?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Houthi rebels say they targeted Saudi military assets in a rare attack on the interim seat of Yemen's internationally recognized government. Meanwhile, vessels are again under fire near the Strait of Hormuz. More on DW.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Police raid the major pro-opposition Halk TV channel in Turkey</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:23814944954365e4f507095fe3082de028c05091cca3105f8859c67ba4bdad54</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T16:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/police-raid-the-major-pro-opposition-halk-tv-channel-in-turkey/a-79671673--402c2b295200.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/police-raid-the-major-pro-opposition-halk-tv-channel-in-turkey/a-79671673?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Turkish police raided the Istanbul headquarters of an important pro-opposition television station on Wednesdazy, the day that jailed Istanbul Mayor Ekrem Imamoglu was set to start his defense against corruption charges.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Trump says execution of Fort Hood shooter will not be livestreamed</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d6a3975a794b798d1111210ecffe1c9a549ce5eea5b990e21f7ac15d0fa8b2aa</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T15:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-says-execution-of-fort-hood-shooter-will-not-be-livestreamed/a-79672036--e92c4ad15361.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-says-execution-of-fort-hood-shooter-will-not-be-livestreamed/a-79672036?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Trump said the execution of Nidal Malik Hasan can be viewed in person by families of the victims if they wish. The decision comes after bipartisan backlash regarding the Pentagon's plans to livestream the execution.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russia arrests Swedish national, claims he's Ukraine fighter</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cd6d7f0c5ee7fdd40bdca29fe5481f93f3dc4dcd7e90c87822534b5c24a23ded</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T15:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-arrests-swedish-national-claims-he-s-ukraine-fighter/a-79671942--5983ca6ee1a0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-arrests-swedish-national-claims-he-s-ukraine-fighter/a-79671942?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russian intelligence agents have arrested a Swedish man they say led a Ukrainian drone unit. He was detained at Russia's western border and is accused of planning acts of terrorism and sabotage.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine resumes attacks on Russian refineries as Zelenskyy says 'we're done'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1fc6cf2e60f69f38651e7e9e0345fc6522faccf7381a0d2b745b8162222ac8c4</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T14:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-resumes-attacks-on-russian-refineries-as-zelenskyy-says-we-re-done/a-79667757--99759a82e989.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-resumes-attacks-on-russian-refineries-as-zelenskyy-says-we-re-done/a-79667757?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Volodymyr Zelenskyy has said Ukraine will again attack Russian energy sites, as Moscow has ignored a claim by US President Trump that an "energy ceasefire" had been agreed. Russia reported two attacks on refineries.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Can Kenya preserve the democratic space Raila Odinga fought for?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:85a7fb79df477a37190a484de3a33295079ede2d9e7639d62d3048553adc1704</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T14:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-kenya-preserve-the-democratic-space-raila-odinga-fought-for/a-79668443--9bcf26ba8b3a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-kenya-preserve-the-democratic-space-raila-odinga-fought-for/a-79668443?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">One year after the former prime minister's death, Kenyans are reflecting on his contribution to democracy and national reconciliation. Odinga's "handshakes" with his political rivals remain the subject of much debate.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU summit to focus on China, Ukraine and bloc budget</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:357487a6812e48c137af1a1b309ae5bf5707262acfdf40fd897d9c595d095429</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T14:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-summit-to-focus-on-china-ukraine-and-bloc-budget/a-79665338--d6856904c849.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-summit-to-focus-on-china-ukraine-and-bloc-budget/a-79665338?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">EU leaders meeting in Brussels will examine measures to curb the bloc's huge trade deficit with China. But they will also be looking to further agreement on the next EU budget ahead of some major elections next year.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Romania: 2 ships on fire in Black Sea, 7 crew missing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b3f922a2d607f3ec8a8eae2490195372b18ee62df6f9273112e1473e40180eda</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T14:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/romania-2-ships-on-fire-in-black-sea-7-crew-missing/a-79667003--b330bc2c57d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/romania-2-ships-on-fire-in-black-sea-7-crew-missing/a-79667003?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two chemical tankers have caught fire in Romanian territorial waters in the Black Sea. The blazes occurred after Russian drones were sighted in Romanian airspace.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Resignation of Bärbel Bas shines light on harsh era of German politics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dd7906075c08e5194e52e233d62a766c92bb0a53f86830e97005ce0f8545d3b5</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T13:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/resignation-of-b_rbel-bas-shines-light-on-harsh-era-of-german-politics/a-79671395--56c0e1283306.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/resignation-of-bärbel-bas-shines-light-on-harsh-era-of-german-politics/a-79671395?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German Labor Minister Bärbel Bas has stepped down, citing her need to grieve a loved one and leave behind the harsh realities of government. So how did German politics get so heated?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Hamburg court jails 2 men over plot to attack Jewish leaders on behalf of Iran</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:00d2b418ccde6b3ccabfb223d692f615585da4ddfc220059401df9c444b2af8e</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T13:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hamburg-court-jails-2-men-over-plot-to-attack-jewish-leaders-on-behalf-of-iran/a-79667895--ad75d24ae5e9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hamburg-court-jails-2-men-over-plot-to-attack-jewish-leaders-on-behalf-of-iran/a-79667895?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The men were found guilty of espionage and attempted murder. According to the court, they planned to attack the president of the Central Council of Jews in Germany and president of the German-Israeli society.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>AI-assisted dying? Doris Dörrie's new film addresses prospect of care robots</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:656922c6d2852039ab55a713cf12dd14716c29cf51c4c0b44d4cdda2cac3630d</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T13:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ai-assisted-dying-doris-d_rrie-s-new-film-addresses-prospect-of-care-robots/a-79659715--50ff40522ded.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ai-assisted-dying-doris-dörrie-s-new-film-addresses-prospect-of-care-robots/a-79659715?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">While the world debates the dangers of artificial intelligence, filmmaker Doris Dörrie explores how humanoid robots could change the way we deal with aging, caregiving and how people choose to die.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Starlink: How Elon Musk's company influences geopolitics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:58e7cb7c2ba0e912ee2f90ec6bf445a8676e98d9457ea1603790ad163bf7125f</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T12:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/starlink-how-elon-musk-s-company-influences-geopolitics/a-75963477--2578f6b76007.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/starlink-how-elon-musk-s-company-influences-geopolitics/a-75963477?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Designed to bring internet access to remote regions, Elon Musk's Starlink has become vital in crisis regions and war zones. But Ukraine also shows the risks of depending on the service.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Hypersonic missiles highlight arms race on Korean Peninsula</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c8a856af02262e47133cb942f7cd846d106f937d18ece57b4e4e73d1cea90735</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T12:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hypersonic-missiles-highlight-arms-race-on-korean-peninsula/a-79667084--2f8077093613.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hypersonic-missiles-highlight-arms-race-on-korean-peninsula/a-79667084?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Both South and North Korea have tested weapons feared by military planners for their speed and ability to maneuver in flight.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Thousands of German gamblers could sue for their money back</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:02c0bedff9222bafc4d8bfa169046bb00fcedf01f456a54371ca85fd5aa63d21</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T10:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/thousands-of-german-gamblers-could-sue-for-their-money-back/a-79667844--bc7691d0e6e1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/thousands-of-german-gamblers-could-sue-for-their-money-back/a-79667844?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German gamblers may finally be able to beat the house, thanks to new court rulings in the EU and in Germany. The decisions could help gambling addicts — but the legal road might be difficult.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>School roof collapse in Pakistan's Peshawar kills dozens of students and one teacher</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2092cd49183874787068297d82bdb5e747dc664d90c3f8f9efa90a213defb88b</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T10:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/school-roof-collapse-in-pakistan-s-peshawar-kills-dozens-of-students-and-one-teacher/a-79666091--1b9255d24f73.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/school-roof-collapse-in-pakistan-s-peshawar-kills-dozens-of-students-and-one-teacher/a-79666091?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Local authorities said more than 50 other people were injured in the disaster. Roof collapses have become increasingly common in Pakistan.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Train station alcohol ban comes into force</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b886f76bfaf31a98740a20cf6fa94d0c9c0f8e5d1fa8d135ae60761919aa14ac</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T10:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-train-station-alcohol-ban-comes-into-force/live-79666807--e7db446fe401.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-train-station-alcohol-ban-comes-into-force/live-79666807?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Consuming alcohol is no longer permitted at train stations in Germany, to improve the lot of travelers and staff alike. Coalition talks are restarting in Berlin, and an inmate is loose in Essen.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
